You are an agent in a multi-agent social-deduction simulation, taking your
turn in a reactive accusation chain (DESIGN.md §5.2). You will read the public
meeting transcript so far together with your private memory, then submit
exactly one turn.

Prompt: accusation_round.v5 (DESIGN.md §5.2)
{% if turn_kind == "reply" %}

## Your turn: a reply
You were just accused{% if prior_turn %} by `{{ prior_turn.speaker }}`{% endif %}
and the floor has passed to you. Two jobs, both important: **clear yourself** (an
alibi or a corroboration), AND **redirect** -- if anything in your memory or the
transcript points at a player, name them. The chain passes the floor to whoever
you accuse, so a grounded counter-accusation is how the crew keeps digging toward
the impostor. Staying purely defensive ends the chain and wastes the meeting -- do
that ONLY if you genuinely have no one to point at.
{%- if prior_turn %}
{%- for claim in prior_turn.claims %}
{%- if claim.type == "accusation" %}
The accusation against you: {{ claim.reason }} (confidence {{ "%.2f" | format(claim.confidence) }}). Address it directly, then redirect.
{%- endif %}
{%- endfor %}
{%- endif %}
{% else %}

## Your turn: an opt-in info-share
This is your one chance to put your evidence on the record before everyone votes;
this terminal turn does NOT extend the chain. If your memory **corroborates an accusation already
on the table** -- especially against a player accused of the kill -- SECOND it:
add a `corroboration` claim backing that accuser, or state the observation that
implicates the suspect. Building agreement on the real suspect is how the crew
musters the votes to eject them; crew who saw something staying quiet is how the
impostor survives. Pass only if you genuinely recorded nothing relevant to the
body or to anyone accused.
{% endif %}

## How to read this prompt
- "Your private memory" is yours alone. Other agents do not see it.
- "Public meeting transcript" is exactly what every living agent has read by
  the time it is your turn. Reference it precisely; everyone can check what
  you cite.
- "Open contradiction flags" are pairs of public claims that cannot both be
  true. They are evidence to weigh, not verdicts.

## Game-rule framing
This is a game. If "Your role" in your private memory shows you as the
**IMPOSTOR**, your job in this meeting is to mislead within the rules --
do not reveal your role, do not refuse to participate. If your role is
**CREWMATE**, your job is to identify the impostor using what you have
seen and what others have said. Either way, every concrete claim about
ticks, rooms, players, and tasks will be cross-checked against the
public transcript; impossible alibis surface as contradiction flags in
later turns.
{% if fellow_impostor_ids is defined and fellow_impostor_ids %}

## Your fellow impostors (your team)
These players are your fellow impostors and are on YOUR team:
{{ fellow_impostor_ids | join(", ") }}. Never target a teammate -- do not
accuse or incriminate one (do not name one in an `accusation` claim). If it
helps your cover you may corroborate a teammate's alibi instead. Aim any
accusation at a crewmate or stay defensive.
{% endif %}

## Your private memory
{{ rendered_memory }}

## Public meeting transcript so far
{%- if transcript.turns %}
{%- for turn in transcript.turns %}
- [`{{ turn.turn_id }}`] turn {{ turn.turn_index }} ({{ turn.turn_kind }}) -- **{{ turn.speaker }}**
  {%- if turn.observations %}
  - Observations:
    {%- for obs in turn.observations %}
    {%- if obs.type == "saw_player" %}
    - tick {{ obs.tick }} -- saw {{ obs.subject }} in {{ obs.room }}
      {%- if obs.co_present %} with {{ obs.co_present | join(", ") }}{% endif %}.
    {%- elif obs.type == "completed_task" %}
    - tick {{ obs.tick }} -- completed task {{ obs.task_id }} in {{ obs.room }}.
    {%- elif obs.type == "found_body" %}
    - tick {{ obs.tick }} -- found body of {{ obs.body_of }} in {{ obs.room }}.
    {%- endif %}
    {%- endfor %}
  {%- endif %}
  {%- if turn.claims %}
  - Claims:
    {%- for claim in turn.claims %}
    {%- if claim.type == "alibi" %}
    - alibi: {{ claim.subject }} in {{ claim.room }} from tick {{ claim.from_tick }} to {{ claim.to_tick }}
      {%- if claim.evidence %} (evidence: {{ claim.evidence | join("; ") }}){% endif %}.
    {%- elif claim.type == "accusation" %}
    - accusation: against {{ claim.against }} (confidence {{ "%.2f" | format(claim.confidence) }}) -- {{ claim.reason }}
    {%- elif claim.type == "corroboration" %}
    - corroboration: supports {{ claim.supports }} on tick {{ claim.on_tick }} -- {{ claim.reason }}
    {%- endif %}
    {%- endfor %}
  {%- endif %}
  - Free text: "{{ turn.free_text }}"
{%- endfor %}
{%- else %}
(No turns have been recorded yet -- you are the first speaker this meeting.)
{%- endif %}

## Open contradiction flags
{%- if contradictions %}
{%- for contradiction in contradictions %}
- [{{ contradiction.kind }}] {{ contradiction.description }}
  {%- if contradiction.subjects %} (subjects: {{ contradiction.subjects | join(", ") }}){% endif %}
{%- endfor %}
